Subject: [PATCH 07904/11362] [outer-loop] FLIP the frontier tier flags ON
 (operator decision) -- verified zero new test failures

SUBMITTED_FRONTIER_TIER_EXHAUSTION_ENABLED     False -> True
SUBMITTED_FRONTIER_TIER_UNIFORM_RANDOM_ENABLED False -> True
SUBMITTED_FRONTIER_TIER_CLICK_VOCAB_ONLY_ENABLED    True (already)
SUBMITTED_FRONTIER_DISTANCE_GRADIENT_ENABLED        False (deliberately NOT flipped -- arm D
  scored 9.67 with dominance 2/3, worse than B2 on both axes; only what earned it was flipped)

EVIDENCE (results/experiment_5836_frontier_definitive.json; 7 arms x 25 games x 3 conditions =
975 cells, 0 errored, reproduction 29/30): arm B2 mean 10.56 wins/cell vs baseline 7.00 (+3.56),
strict PER-SEED dominance in 8 of 9 (condition x seed) cells, holding 10.00 / 10.67 / 11.00 across
real / recoloured / reflected. Its one loss (cd82) is a diagnosed budget WALL, not lost capability.
The click gate's contribution is isolated by B2 vs B2_nofix: dominance 8/9 vs 3/9, tu93 lost 0/9
vs 6/9. Full rationale + the honest limit live AT the flag.

HONEST LIMIT, recorded at the flag: public-game evidence via the offline dev twin. The positive
control (arm E, just-explore through our shim) scored 6.67 -- BELOW our own baseline -- so by the
A/B's own pre-registered rule the harness is the confound for any cross-implementation claim, and
none is made. The flip rests on the INTERNAL A-vs-B2-vs-B2_nofix comparison (same explorer, flags
differ), i.e. a capability argument, NOT demonstrated hidden-game transfer.

REGRESSION VERIFICATION -- and the first attempt at it was WRONG, which matters:
A worktree-at-HEAD baseline reported 63 failures vs 46 post-flip and 'zero new failures'. That
comparison was invalid: the worktree lacks the main tree's uncommitted artifact state, so a
flip-caused failure could hide behind a baseline artifact failure. The clean control -- SAME tree,
identical artifacts, flags reverted via env -- found 46 vs 46 with 2 NEW failures masked by 2
fixed ones. Comparing TOTALS would have shipped a regression; comparing failure SETS caught it.
Both were brittle exact-dict assertions on candidate rows, which now carry an additive 'tier'
annotation (exp4512 imitation action prior, exp4513 adaptive per-step budget) -- correct action,
data and truncation throughout, so no behavioural regression. Assertions now check the meaningful
fields and pass in BOTH flag states.
FINAL: flags ON 44 failed / 7528 passed; flags OFF 46 failed / 7526 passed; ON-minus-OFF = ZERO new
failures. The only OFF-state failures are the two guard tests now correctly asserting the ON default.

Three guard tests updated rather than bypassed -- they existed to force a conscious, recorded
decision before a flip, which is what they did. The flags-off pop(0) byte-identity property is
PRESERVED (requested explicitly), because it is what makes the B2_nofix attribution arm valid.

